  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "RenderMark — professional markdown rendering, export, and publishing.\n\nUse these tools when the user needs styled output from markdown (PDF, DOCX, HTML, images, hosted pages). Do NOT use for plain markdown editing or general writing.\n\n## Tool Selection Guide\n- Preview styled markdown → render_markdown\n- Export to file (PDF/DOCX/HTML) → export_markdown\n- Export multiple files → export_batch\n- Create PNG/JPEG image → render_to_image\n- Publish to web with shareable link → publish_to_rendermark\n- Publish as Google Doc → publish_to_google_docs\n- Share with specific people → share_document (after publishing)\n- Temporary preview link → share_live_preview\n- Compare two versions → render_diff\n- Check quality before publishing → validate_markdown\n- Import from GitHub → sync_from_github\n- Learn RenderMark workflow guidance → get_rendermark_instructions\n\n## Key Workflows\n- \"Share this doc\" → publish_to_rendermark, then share_document with emails\n- \"Export all docs\" → export_batch with glob pattern\n- \"Sync from GitHub\" → sync_from_github with owner/repo/path\n\n## Themes & Features\nThemes: default (clean sans-serif), dark, serif (academic), minimal.\nTemplates: report, meeting-notes, memo, letter, slides, changelog.\nExtensions: Mermaid diagrams, KaTeX math, syntax highlighting, frontmatter, task lists, footnotes.\n\n## Best Practices\n- Always include a title when publishing or exporting\n- Pass github context ({ owner, repo, branch, path }) for GitHub READMEs so relative images resolve\n- Prefer publish_to_rendermark over export_markdown when user says \"share\"\n- Run validate_markdown on important documents before publishing\n- Table of contents is on by default; set showToc: false to disable",
  "durationMs": 17197,
